WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:18.249
"Nora!" Maggie called. "Stop!"

2
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.787
Nora looked over at them. Then she ran away.

3
00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:25.161
"Hey," Henry exclaimed in surprise.

4
00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:28.335
"Catch her!" Cole took off after Nora.

5
00:00:28.336 --> 00:00:31.673
Henry followed, with Maggie right beside him.

6
00:00:31.674 --> 00:00:34.547
Nora was surprisingly fast for a little kid.

7
00:00:34.548 --> 00:00:38.784
She turned into a booth filled with pottery.

8
00:00:38.785 --> 00:00:43.979
"Careful," Maggie exclaimed as The Lemonade Detectives ran into the booth behind her.

9
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.833
"This stuff looks breakable."

10
00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:50.487
Just ahead Nora scooted under a low table full of vases.

11
00:00:50.488 --> 00:00:55.806
"We can't fit under there," cried Henry. "We'll have to go around!"

12
00:00:55.807 --> 00:00:58.850
Cole had already dashed out of the booth.

13
00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:02.679
Henry and Maggie followed as Cole sprinted after Nora.

14
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.899
"Nora, stop!" Maggie yelled. "We just want to talk to you!"

15
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:13.470
"There she goes." Cole pointed. Nora was ducking into another booth.

16
00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:17.381
Maggie ran after her. Henry and Cole followed.

17
00:01:17.382 --> 00:01:20.106
They found themselves in a quilting booth.

18
00:01:20.107 --> 00:01:25.993
"Hey, what are you kids doing?" a woman exclaimed. "This isn't a playground!"

19
00:01:25.994 --> 00:01:31.714
"Sorry," Henry said breathlessly. Then he ran out of the booth after Nora.

20
00:01:31.715 --> 00:01:36.108
She was heading out of the crafts fair and across the central part of the park.

21
00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:40.327
She ducked between two people waiting in line to buy hot dogs.

22
00:01:40.328 --> 00:01:44.361
"Excuse me," Henry said, trying to push after her.

23
00:01:44.362 --> 00:01:48.456
"Hey! Get in the back of the line!" one of the customers said.

24
00:01:48.457 --> 00:01:53.162
"We're just passing through," Maggie said. Then she pointed at Nora.

25
00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:56.020
"We need to catch that little girl!"

26
00:01:56.021 --> 00:02:01.262
"Oh, why didn't you say so?" the customer grumbled, finally moving aside.

27
00:02:01.263 --> 00:02:04.271
For a second Henry thought they'd lost Nora.

28
00:02:04.272 --> 00:02:07.006
Then he spotted her running into the art show.

29
00:02:07.007 --> 00:02:10.018
She ducked behind the nearest display.

30
00:02:10.019 --> 00:02:13.884
"Hurry!" Henry called to his friends, running after Nora.

31
00:02:13.885 --> 00:02:18.752
"We have to—oof!" He crashed into someone.

32
00:02:18.753 --> 00:02:23.321
"Hey," a familiar voice said. "Watch where you're going!"

33
00:02:23.322 --> 00:02:24.923
It was Hannah!

34
00:02:24.924 --> 00:02:28.396
"What are you doing here?" Maggie sounded surprised.

35
00:02:28.397 --> 00:02:33.956
"I decided to go for a walk," Hannah replied. "It's a free country."

36
00:02:33.957 --> 00:02:39.322
"Okay," Henry said. "We're just surprised to see you here."

37
00:02:39.323 --> 00:02:43.719
"Yeah. We thought you didn't like the art show," Cole added.

38
00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.107
Hannah shrugged. "Does that mean I'm not allowed to walk past it?"

39
00:02:48.108 --> 00:02:53.736
"No," Henry said. "But it makes you look a little suspicious."

40
00:02:53.737 --> 00:02:59.896
Maggie nodded. "I bet she's trying to sabotage the whole art show by stealing the best painting!"

41
00:02:59.897 --> 00:03:04.889
"What?" Hannah exclaimed. "No way, I wouldn't do that!"

42
00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.768
"Are you sure?" Cole said.

43
00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:11.943
"You acted pretty weird when we mentioned Nathan's painting earlier.

44
00:03:11.944 --> 00:03:15.389
And a few minutes later, it disappeared!"

45
00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:19.149
"I didn't take it." Hannah didn't sound annoyed anymore.

46
00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.585
"I'd never do that. Nathan's really talented.

47
00:03:23.586 --> 00:03:26.905
He deserves to win that spot in the museum!"

48
00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:33.028
She sounded sincere. "Why would you care about his painting?" Henry asked.

49
00:03:33.029 --> 00:03:35.249
"I thought you didn't like art."

50
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.403
"That's not true," Hannah said quickly. "Actually, I love art."

51
00:03:40.404 --> 00:03:43.950
"Huh?" Maggie looked confused. "But you said—"

52
00:03:43.951 --> 00:03:46.300
"I know," Hannah interrupted.

53
00:03:46.301 --> 00:03:50.386
"I was just mad because I couldn't enter the art show myself."

54
00:03:50.387 --> 00:03:53.475
"You were going to enter?" Cole asked.

55
00:03:53.476 --> 00:03:57.466
Hannah nodded. "I like basket weaving.

56
00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:03.140
But I'm not crazy about it like my parents are. I'm a sculptor."

57
00:04:03.141 --> 00:04:05.379
"Really?" Henry said.

58
00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:09.691
"Yes. Want to see my latest sculpture?" Hannah asked shyly.

59
00:04:09.692 --> 00:04:12.360
"I have pictures of it on my phone."

60
00:04:12.361 --> 00:04:14.779
"Sure," Henry said.

61
00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:19.479
Hannah pulled out her phone and showed Henry and the others photos of her sculpture.

62
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.548
It was of a girl holding a cat.

63
00:04:22.549 --> 00:04:26.526
"Wow," Cole said. "You're really good!"

64
00:04:26.527 --> 00:04:32.392
"Thanks." Hannah sounded sad. "I wanted to enter the art show this year.

65
00:04:32.393 --> 00:04:38.743
But my family was so busy getting ready for the crafts fair, I didn't have much time to sculpt.

66
00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:41.845
So my piece wasn't ready in time."

67
00:04:41.846 --> 00:04:45.848
"That's why you sounded mad earlier," Henry guessed.

68
00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:49.701
"I guess I was jealous." Hannah sighed.

69
00:04:49.702 --> 00:04:54.523
"But I wouldn't steal another artist's work—I promise."

70
00:04:54.524 --> 00:04:58.581
Henry believed her. He could tell his friends did too.

71
00:04:58.582 --> 00:05:03.220
"Thanks for showing us your sculpture," he said, handing back Hannah's phone.

72
00:05:03.221 --> 00:05:05.466
"Sorry we suspected you."

73
00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:10.792
"It's okay," Hannah said. "I don't blame you. I was acting weird."

74
00:05:10.793 --> 00:05:15.617
"You sure were," Maggie told her. "But I understand why now."

75
00:05:15.618 --> 00:05:20.233
Hannah smiled. "Want to watch the judging with me?" she asked.

76
00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:24.096
"I figure that will help me get inspired to enter next year."

77
00:05:24.097 --> 00:05:29.709
"Sorry, we can't," Cole said. "We still have to solve the mystery."

78
00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:35.931
"Yeah," Henry said. "We need to track down . . . Nora!" he shouted.

79
00:05:35.932 --> 00:05:39.132
The little girl was tiptoeing past them again.

80
00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:42.078
She heard Henry yell and started running.

81
00:05:42.079 --> 00:05:47.559
Maggie leaped forward and grabbed Nora's arm before the little girl could duck under the next display.

82
00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.161
"Got her!" Maggie exclaimed.

83
00:05:50.162 --> 00:05:55.802
Nora burst into tears. "I'm sorry!" she wailed.

84
00:05:55.803 --> 00:06:02.709
"I only took it because of Patches!"
